            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Shannon"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I tossed my baby spinach in garlic-infused olive oil so the leaves would be more evenly coated once in the saute pan. I also splashed in a little seasoned vinegar, garlic powder and a pinch of sea salt. I found 10 minutes was too long for the texture I wanted, so next time, I'll simply heat through (4-5 minutes). I added this spinach, along with some roasted cherry tomatoes, into pesto-tossed angel hair pasta and topped with parmesan cheese. Delish! Will make again with my modifications.",
            "datePublished": "2013-01-22T07:06:54.410Z"
          },
          {
